          |__| W I R E L E S S   F R E E D O M
 -----------------------------------------------------

This is the buildsystem for the OpenWrt Linux distribution.

To build your own firmware you need a Linux, BSD or MacOSX system (case
sensitive filesystem required). Cygwin is unsupported because of the lack
of a case sensitive file system.

You need gcc, binutils, bzip2, flex, python, perl, make, find, grep, diff,
unzip, gawk, getopt, subversion, libz-dev and libc headers installed.

1. Run "./scripts/feeds update -a" to obtain all the latest package definitions
defined in feeds.conf / feeds.conf.default

2. Run "./scripts/feeds install -a" to install symlinks for all obtained
packages into package/feeds/

3. Run "make menuconfig" to select your preferred configuration for the
toolchain, target system & firmware packages.

4. Run "make" to build your firmware. This will download all sources, build
the cross-compile toolchain and then cross-compile the Linux kernel & all
chosen applications for your target system.

Sunshine!
	Your OpenWrt Community
	http://www.openwrt.org

# OpenWrt 19.07.10 Modernized

A modernized and maintained build of **OpenWrt 19.07.10** adapted for building on modern Linux hosts and contemporary GCC/Python toolchains.

This repository is based on the original OpenWrt 19.07.10 source tree and contains compatibility fixes required to build this legacy release with a modern development environment.

The goal is to keep the original OpenWrt 19.07.10 target platform usable while minimizing changes to the original OpenWrt architecture and build system.

## Why this repository exists

OpenWrt 19.07.10 is a legacy release and its original build system predates modern Linux distributions and current compiler versions.

When building it on a modern host, several components fail because of changes in:

* GCC diagnostics and language defaults
* newer C/C++ compiler behavior
* Python 3
* modern CMake
* modern system headers
* stricter compiler warnings
* changes in bundled third-party build tools

This repository contains compatibility fixes for those problems.

## Base version

* OpenWrt: **19.07.10**
* Linux kernel: **4.14.275**
* Target example: **Atheros AR71xx / MIPS 24Kc**
* Example device: **Linksys WRT160NL**
* libc: **musl**

## Modernization changes

### GCC 15/16 compatibility

Several legacy components fail with current GCC versions because warnings and language behavior have become stricter.

Compatibility changes were added for:

* GCC 16 `nodiscard` attribute handling in `m4`
* legacy C code relying on implicit declarations
* old C/C++ constructs rejected by modern compilers
* stricter compiler diagnostics

### Python 3 build support

Legacy OpenWrt build tools contain Python 2-era assumptions.

The SCons Python wrapper was updated to use Python 3, allowing the legacy build system to operate on systems where Python 2 is no longer available.

### pkg-config / GLib

The bundled `pkg-config` build was adjusted for modern GCC by explicitly using a GNU C standard compatible with the legacy source.

### e2fsprogs

Host compilation was adjusted to use a compatible GNU C language standard with modern GCC.

### libelf

The host build was adjusted to pass modern compiler flags correctly and tolerate legacy implicit declarations that would otherwise be treated as fatal errors.

### CMake

OpenWrt 19.07.10 contains an old CMake version.

Compatibility patches were added for modern compilers, including:

* disabling the problematic GHS bootstrap path
* fixing missing `cstdint` usage in the worker pool implementation

### GMP

The host build configuration was adjusted for compatibility with modern host toolchains.

### bc

Compatibility fixes were added for modern system headers, including `ptrdiff_t` handling.

### jsonfilter

The bundled Lemon parser code contains old-style declarations that conflict with modern compiler behavior.

Explicit function prototypes were added to allow jsonfilter to compile with modern GCC.

### squashfs / squashfskit4

Legacy signal-handler declarations were updated to match modern compiler expectations.

### iproute2 / libcap

The legacy OpenWrt package definitions for `ip-full` and `tc` referenced `libcap`.

The dependency was removed so these packages can be built without requiring the unavailable legacy `libcap` package in this OpenWrt 19.07.10 tree.

The existing optional capability detection in iproute2 remains separate from the OpenWrt package dependency.

## Design goals

This repository intentionally does **not** attempt to port OpenWrt 19.07.10 into a completely new OpenWrt release.

The goal is instead:

1. Keep the original OpenWrt 19.07.10 base.
2. Make the build work with modern host systems.
3. Keep changes small and isolated.
4. Avoid unnecessary changes to target-side OpenWrt behavior.
5. Make the repository reusable as a base for other projects.

Project-specific applications and packages should remain outside this repository.

For example, NREPlatform uses this repository as its OpenWrt base:

```text
NREPlatform
└── openwrt-19.07.10
        ↓
    openwrt-19.07.10-modernized
```

## Building

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/skye7x/openwrt-19.07.10-modernized.git
cd openwrt-19.07.10-modernized
```

Configure the target:

```bash
make menuconfig
```

Then build:

```bash
make -j$(nproc)
```

For verbose builds:

```bash
make -j$(nproc) V=s
```

## Linksys WRT160NL

The repository has been tested by building OpenWrt 19.07.10 for:

* Target System: `Atheros AR7xxx/AR9xxx`
* Subtarget: `Generic`
* Target Profile: `Linksys WRT160NL`
* Architecture: `mips_24kc`
* Kernel: `4.14.275`

Example output:

```text
bin/targets/ar71xx/generic/
├── openwrt-ar71xx-generic-wrt160nl-squashfs-factory.bin
└── openwrt-ar71xx-generic-wrt160nl-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
```

## NREPlatform

This repository is used as the modernized OpenWrt base for the NREPlatform project.

NREPlatform adds a separate OpenWrt package containing the NRE daemon and its procd service integration.

The NRE package itself is intentionally **not part of this repository**.

Repository:

```text
https://github.com/skye7x/NREPlatform
```

## Scope

This project focuses on keeping the legacy OpenWrt 19.07.10 build system usable on modern development hosts.

It is not intended to replace newer OpenWrt releases.

Use newer OpenWrt releases when hardware support and project requirements allow it. This repository exists for projects that specifically need the OpenWrt 19.07.10 base or legacy target support.

## Status

The modernization work has been validated by successfully building OpenWrt 19.07.10 for the Linksys WRT160NL, including:

* kernel
* target packages
* root filesystem
* squashfs images
* factory image
* sysupgrade image

